1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,500
Meet Things. A little helping hand that turns your voice into real computer actions.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Press the shortcut. Then just speak.

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:19,000
Find three research papers about retrieval augmented generation. Open the sources and give me a short summary with links.

4
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:25,000
That's the whole request. It starts automatically. No typing, and no send button.

5
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:32,000
Things opens its own browser and visits public research sources.

6
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:43,000
It reads the page, captures the screen, and decides what to do next. Then it checks the result before continuing.

7
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:49,000
This part is sped up. The sources and AI actions are real.

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:01,000
And here's the result. Three research papers, short summaries, and source links you can open and verify.

9
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,000
From one spoken request to a research shortlist, without manually searching through tabs.

10
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Things. A little hand. A lot off your hands.
